== C. Structure: the 3/8 plateau (k = 24) and the level k = 27 ==
  [ok] k = 24 lies on the plateau (rho* = 3/8)
  [ok] C1. the 7x+1 cycle (-169, -548, -274, -137, -436, -218, -109, -338)/87 (shape (8,3), 2^8 - 7^3 = -87, density 3/8) is a cycle of the certified optimal sign strategy at k = 24, and every edge of it is tight for the certified potential psi
  [ok] C2. lower certificate at k = 24: tight core of 38044 pairs; Min's best responses against the certified Max strategy (tight cycles) all have density exactly 3/8, with shapes [(8, 3), (24, 9), (32, 12), (40, 15), (48, 18), (56, 21), (64, 24)]; the (8,3) ones are rational cycles with denominators dividing 87; all are real-bounded (|x| <= 170)
C3. census of the simple rational cycles of small shape kept by the certified optimal strategies (a cycle is kept iff sigma agrees with its sign at the residue of each of its odd points):
    k=24 (rho* = 3/8): (2,1) exp 0/2, (5,2) exp 0/8, (7,3) exp 0/38, (8,3) exp 4/54, (13,5) exp 0/3164, (11,4) exp 61/480, (14,5) exp 374/4568
    k=27 (rho* = 35/94): (2,1) exp 0/2, (5,2) exp 0/8, (7,3) exp 0/38, (8,3) exp 0/54, (13,5) exp 0/3164, (11,4) exp 33/480, (14,5) exp 323/4568
  [ok] every simple cycle of density > rho* among these shapes is broken (as it must be), the plateau strategy keeps 4 of the 54 simple (8,3)-cycles, and at k = 27 none of them; hundreds of expanding (14,5)-cycles (7^5 > 2^14, density 5/14 = 0.35714) survive in these optimal strategies, while a class-(i) strategy would have to break all 4568 of them
C4. the rational relaxation: the real-sign assignment sigma(x) = sgn(x) keeps no expanding cycle (Proposition S of the note, proved by hand); exhaustive check over all simple cycles of 7x+-1 with p <= 11:
  [ok] 24653 expanding simple cycles (p <= 11): sgn keeps none; 395 contracting ones: sgn keeps 132 (e.g. the free cycle (1, 4, 2)); so no finite set of rational cycles obstructs provability at every level

